      "message": "specifications: Group device measurements ABI arguments\n\nThe `sbi_covg_get_device_measurements` ecall currently passes the SPDM\n`GET_MEASUREMENTS` request parameters as flat scalar arguments: a nonce\nbuffer address, a request attribute word, an output buffer address, and\nan output size. On RV32 with Sv32 paging, physical addresses are 34 bits\nwide while `unsigned long` is only 32 bits. Issue #172 requires every\nPA-bearing argument to be split into `_lo`/`_hi` register pairs to avoid\ntruncation in highmem configurations.\n\nNaively expanding the two PA arguments of this ecall would yield seven\nargument slots, which overflows the six SBI argument registers (a0-a5).\n\nConsolidate the nonce buffer and request attributes into a single\nin-memory request descriptor, referenced by a single PA argument. This\nfollows the pattern already used elsewhere in this spec for the IDE\nstream descriptor (`sbi_covh_connect_device`) and the IDE key descriptor\n(`sbi_covt_program_rp_ide_key`), and leaves enough argument-register\nheadroom for the subsequent lo/hi PA split (to be done in a follow-up\ncommit).\n\nThe `Nonce == 0x0` sentinel used by the previous ABI to request\nTSM-generated nonces is replaced by an all-zero 32-byte `Nonce` field in\nthe descriptor, which is expressible without relying on a pointer-level\nsentinel.\n\nFixes #172\n\nSigned-off-by: Samuel Ortiz <sameo@meta.com>",
